# Coord Helper API

See [README Coord Helper API](../../README.md#coord-helper-api) for the full model.

## When to use

Prefer `self.coordHelper(event.local, event.treeUuid).inner()…` over repeated `childSegAtCoord` / `childCardAtCoord` when:

- descending more than one nested level along a local coordinate
- folding attrs into an object with `fold` / `get()`
- drag `updateAttrs` / slot resolve (e.g. WeekSeg → WeekdaySeg → HourSeg)

Use raw `childSegAtCoord(coord, treeUuid)` for a single optional lookup that may return `undefined`.

## Call-site rules

- Call `coordHelper(coord, treeUuid)` on the node that owns `coord` (typically `self` in a mouse handler). Do not call it on an ancestor with a child-relative local.
- Pass an explicit `treeUuid` — required for multi-widget mounts. Do not use first-Vi helpers. From a card handler targeting a place seg on an axis, pass `event.widgetTreeUuids.horizontal` or `.vertical` as appropriate.
- `inner()` throws when no Vi or nested child covers the coordinate (fluent types stay non-optional). When a miss should yield `undefined` (e.g. drag outside the grid), wrap the chain in `try/catch`.
- Do not annotate callbacks with `any`. Prefer implicit typing so `GenSegments` / `GenCards` and `ECollectionItemType<T["nested"]>` apply.
- `fold` callbacks must return an object literal with parentheses: `(seg) => ({ field: … })`.
- Do not hand-roll nested `childSegAtCoord` plus local offset arithmetic for multi-level walks.

## Segments

```typescript
weekSeg.coordHelper(event.local, event.treeUuid)  // CoordHelper<WeekSeg>
  .inner()                                        // CoordHelper<WeekdaySeg>
  .peek((weekdaySeg) => { … })
  .inner()                                        // CoordHelper<HourSeg>
  .getSeg();

weekSeg.coordHelper(event.local, event.treeUuid)
  .inner()
  .fold((weekdaySeg) => ({ weekDay: weekdaySeg.attrs.weekday.number }))
  .inner()
  .fold((hourSeg) => ({ hour: hourSeg.attrs.hour }))
  .get();
```

Classes: `CoordHelper`, `CoordBasedFold` in `xorlab/src/facade/CoordHelper.ts`.

## Cards

```typescript
listCard.coordHelper(event.local, event.treeUuid)  // CardCoordHelper<…>
  .inner()
  .getCard();

listCard.coordHelper(event.local, event.treeUuid)
  .inner()
  .fold((card) => ({ id: card.attrs.id }))
  .get();
```

Classes: `CardCoordHelper`, `CardCoordBasedFold` in `xorlab/src/facade/CardCoordHelper.ts`.
